{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771556-fenris-ur-goals-in-basra-iraq","id":771556,"title":"Fenris-Ur Goals in Basra, Iraq","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-22T09:53:50-08:00","id":771556,"title":"Fenris-Ur Goals in Basra, Iraq","content":"Heads up for my players if you guys read these forums, reading this thread may ruin my game for you if I go through with a hunt that leads to Basra!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now that that is out of the way. I was reading the write up for Basra, Iraq\u200b and I throughout the whole thing I was under the impression that Fenris-Ur's purpose in Iraq is to awaken Dana-Ur and fill the part of itself that is missing. But since Fenris-Ur doesn't know what is missing (Dana-Ur) it is acting on instinct, and probably doesn't even actually have the plans for the Ghost Wolves, Fenris-Ur just knows it needs them.<br /> <br /> Now assuming that Dana-Ur is also a first born, that makes it a known First Born without a tribe, and there is a convenient population of Ghost Wolves in Basra that can form a Tribe, if they locate Dana-Ur.<br /> <br /> This got me thinking if the Ghost Wolves find Dana-Ur what would Creator Wolf's &quot;trial&quot; be? and what would the resulting tribe be like? So far all my only ideas is to make the preferred prey either Maeljin, or the Shadow itself. In particular things like Shoal's (unless someone can argue why they are a good), Wounds, Barrens, or other such &quot;corruptions&quot; in the shadow, and maybe even corruptions of the &quot;flesh&quot; (like heavily polluted region).<br /> <br /> I have no ideas what their culture, oath, or anything else would be like. So I was hoping we could get some ideas together! (Maybe even come up with a better idea for Preferred Prey. Since Preferred Prey don't have to be things, the Pure write ups in the Core gives us conceptual things like: those that dishonour or disrespect the shadow, the &quot;tainted&quot;, and those that refuse to honor the hunt.)<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat we have got so far:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Favored Prey: \u200b&quot;Those who've lingered to go long&quot;, &quot;that which has lingered too long&quot;, or &quot;Those who are obsolete&quot;<br /> Renown: Purity or Cunning<br /> Gifts: \u200bInspiration, Warding, or Shaping<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":4737,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","user":"Afro Luigi","date":".  Updated Spoiler Section 12-20-2015, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T10:12:52-08:00","id":771573,"title":"","content":"I could see rescuing Creator Wolf and rebuilding the wreck of Basra as a good one. As for a sacred prey, why not Angels?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T11:15:35-08:00","id":771613,"title":"","content":"Ephemeral beings are already covered by the Bone Shadows. Make it undead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T12:22:51-08:00","id":771645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771556-fenris-ur-goals-in-basra-iraq?p=771613#post771613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ephemeral beings are already covered by the Bone Shadows. Make it undead.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ravening Wolf and the Eaters of the Dead would like to have a word with you...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T12:50:12-08:00","id":771660,"title":"","content":"It doesn't have to be limited to Angels, but all of the God Machine spawned things. Angels, Demons, stigmatics, cults. The write-up, to me, made it seem like the God Machine was somehow involved with the imprisonment of Danu-Ur, or with Danu-Ur itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T13:13:33-08:00","id":771671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771556-fenris-ur-goals-in-basra-iraq?p=771660#post771660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't have to be limited to Angels, but all of the God Machine spawned things. Angels, Demons, stigmatics, cults. The write-up, to me, made it seem like the God Machine was somehow involved with the imprisonment of Danu-Ur, or with Danu-Ur itself.</div> </div> </div> </div> Odd, I got the exact opposite impression, that Creator wolf was sleeping. But I just reread it and saw the reference to half finished Construction Projects and Chimeric Spirits. So now I see where you are coming from.<br /> <br /> But I thought Angels, Ghosts, and Spirits operated on different frequencies. And are different enough that a Werewolf meeting a GM Angel would go &quot;this is weird&quot;, and realize it's ephemeral but not a spirit.<br /> <br /> Also I just Ctrl+F'ed Creator Wolf and found this passage in the Blood Talons write up<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf the Forsaken - Second Edition, page 34</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThis story is true. In the time before, when Father Wolf led his children in the hunt, Fenris-Ur had a twin Danu-Ur, she was called, the Creator Wolf. She alone could calm her brother's rages and convince him to quit the field. He alone could drive off the chattering spirits that swarmed around her and threatened to drive her mad. They were in balance then, but the Father's death tore them asunder. Now the Destroyer rages without end, and the Creator gibbers rapidly and spreads her madness like a plague.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So those &quot;Construction projects&quot; and Chimeric Creatures could be constructs from Creator Wolf, or the Spirits that are driving her mad. So at least we have the challenge for the Ghost Wolves. To drive those spirits off, and bring peace to her &quot;Place that is not&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T13:18:14-08:00","id":771676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Afro Luigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771556-fenris-ur-goals-in-basra-iraq?p=771671#post771671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I thought Angels, Ghosts, and Spirits operated on different frequencies. And are different enough that a Werewolf meeting a GM Angel would go &quot;this is weird&quot;, and realize it's ephemeral but not a spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right, though the idea could be that the tribe teaches its members about the difference when teaching why it's important to hunt them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T13:23:35-08:00","id":771683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771556-fenris-ur-goals-in-basra-iraq?p=771676#post771676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's right, though the idea could be that the tribe teaches its members about the difference when teaching why it's important to hunt them.</div> </div> </div> </div> It is an interesting idea, but I'd be hesitant to use it. I'd personally like to keep it Crossover lite, so that the tribe can be used in a game that only uses the Werewolf books and not any Demon books or the God-Machine Chronicles. And in a Crossover game stick Angels into the Bone Shadow domain, and the Stigmatics, and Cults into the Iron Master domain.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T13:30:38-08:00","id":771688,"title":"","content":"How about the Idigam? Just reading the little snippet of text made me think of them.<br /> <br /> I mean, if your game involves the creation of a new tribe, that really should herald a major change in the setting. The basic setup of the present setting is that the Uratha are having massive problems dealing with the Idigam; the creation/revival of a tribe that can specifically combat them seems a pretty great way to end a chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T13:46:16-08:00","id":771695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771556-fenris-ur-goals-in-basra-iraq?p=771688#post771688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about the Idigam? Just reading the little snippet of text made me think of them.<br /> <br /> I mean, if your game involves the creation of a new tribe, that really should herald a major change in the setting. The basic setup of the present setting is that the Uratha are having massive problems dealing with the Idigam; the creation/revival of a tribe that can specifically combat them seems a pretty great way to end a chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div> Has awesome as that would be, it's not what I'm trying to do here. I'm trying to create a whole new tribe that can be used in the future by anyone (my players and people here on the forum), and not just an endgame thing.<br /> <br /> My game actually won't be featuring as a main enemy instead:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It's going to deal with the weird things in the shadow, and material. I'll be making heavy use of War Against the Pure, Skinchangers, and the Werewolf Night Horrors book. An Idigam may be showing up though.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'd much rather this end up being useful for any game, and not have it end games prematurely, because the ST wants to run a game featuring an Idigam and a player wants to join the Creator Wolf Tribe.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T14:10:47-08:00","id":771709,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify, your game is going to be set after the events of the Basra setting?<br /> <br /> I mean, I presented it as an endgame because I thought you wanted to play through the Basra setting. It certainly doesn't have to be the end. Playing through the new tribes wars on the Idigam could be really fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T14:19:39-08:00","id":771714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771556-fenris-ur-goals-in-basra-iraq?p=771709#post771709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify, your game is going to be set after the events of the Basra setting?<br /> <br /> I mean, I presented it as an endgame because I thought you wanted to play through the Basra setting. It certainly doesn't have to be the end. Playing through the new tribes wars on the Idigam could be really fun.</div> </div> </div> </div> I haven't really decided yet, it may be before, during and after. Or it just may be after, and they'll be hearing about this new Tribe. I also want to be able to use this Tribe in Future games, which will be set after Basra will be resolved.\u200b And of course I want other people here on the forums to be able to use it as well in any games.<br /> <br /> P.S. I may just ignore Basra completely for my game, or my players may ignore the plot points and not even care. I'm designing this game to be a sandbox so if the PCs want to ignore a bunch of plot points I'll be fine and let them resolve themselves.. They may have to clean up that resolution, but I don't want them to be dire threats.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T14:35:42-08:00","id":771727,"title":"","content":"I'd recommend an oath to do with clearing space for things to grow (or be built or etc) and have the non-unique Shadow Gifts be Inspiration and Shaping or Warding. Perhaps make their sacred prey &quot;those who've lingered too long.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T14:52:13-08:00","id":771738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771556-fenris-ur-goals-in-basra-iraq?p=771645#post771645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ravening Wolf and the Eaters of the Dead would like to have a word with you...</div> </div> </div> </div>I frankly don't give a damn about your custom tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T15:05:34-08:00","id":771747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771556-fenris-ur-goals-in-basra-iraq?p=771727#post771727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd recommend an oath to do with clearing space for things to grow (or be built or etc) and have the non-unique Shadow Gifts be Inspiration and Shaping or Warding. Perhaps make their sacred prey &quot;those who've lingered too long.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> I really like this! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Although I am tempted to reword it to &quot;that which has lingered too long&quot; so it covers institutions, customs, buildings, and beings. And then the Oath talks about how it's their duty to fill in the gaps, \u200bso we can keep some synergy with Destroyer Wolf.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar576_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"576\" data-vbnamecard=\"576\">Ephsy</a> (Can't get the quote function to let me quote multiple people): Ravening Wolf and Eaters of the Dead are from the lodges write up in Second Edition. They want to form their own tribe.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T15:05:51-08:00","id":771748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I frankly don't give a damn about your custom tribes. </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate? I mean, those are both from 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T15:07:06-08:00","id":771751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771556-fenris-ur-goals-in-basra-iraq?p=771738#post771738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I frankly don't give a damn about your custom tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, sorry for not being clear. The Eaters of the Dead aren't a custom Tribe, but a canon Lodge in 2E Core. They seek to become a Tribe by seeking out a Firstborn they name Ravening Wolf[EDIT: aka Isim-Ur], and claim the Undead as their Sacred Prey. Again, sorry for being unclear.<br /> <br /> EDIT: They're on Pages 52 and 53, if that helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":".  Added info 11-22-2015, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T18:03:01-08:00","id":771946,"title":"","content":"Indeed, the Eaters of the Dead are very much not a custom Tribe. Expect more material on the <i>Ki Anagh </i>in the future.<i>\u200b</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T20:13:32-08:00","id":772029,"title":"","content":"What I don't understand is why it is now possible for a new tribal totem to be added to the werewolves, but it hasn't in the thousands of years werewolves have existed. I like the idea of Ghost Wolves taking a forgotten first born or a modern wolf spirit and making it into a new tribal totem, but it would be cool to see examples of such having already been created sometimes in one of the historical settings, even if that tribe were later wiped out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T20:20:04-08:00","id":772034,"title":"","content":"TO be fair, the Uratha largely want patrons who have spiritual ties to the Wolf, and therefore jive with the Siskur-Dah. We don't know how many spiritual 'children' the Wolf had outside the nine, and the Firstborn are pretty big and badass spirits who are tied to concepts that aren't going away anytime soon. We probably haven't seen many tribe options spring up simply because the pool is limited, and we haven't seen any die because the patrons themselves are really fragging hard to kill meaningfully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T22:04:52-08:00","id":772079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771556-fenris-ur-goals-in-basra-iraq?p=772029#post772029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I don't understand is why it is now possible for a new tribal totem to be added to the werewolves, but it hasn't in the thousands of years werewolves have existed. I like the idea of Ghost Wolves taking a forgotten first born or a modern wolf spirit and making it into a new tribal totem, but it would be cool to see examples of such having already been created sometimes in one of the historical settings, even if that tribe were later wiped out.</div> </div> </div> </div> Have we ever been given an actual timeline of when the Tribes were created? In the Sumer (set about 4,000 years ago judging by the reference to Gudea of Lagash) write up in the Chroniclers guide the only mention of Tribes is in the Character Creation portion, so they weren't a big part of Bau politics (and could be dropped entirely). And the Neolithic Age (which ended about 4,000-6,000 years ago) was when Father Wolf was running around apparently (according to teasers from The Dark Eras). I'd say the tribes are under 4,000 years old.<br /> <br /> Since Spirits don't have a life expectancy we can safely assume that if there were more then 8 First Born, the others are still around. And across various books we have references <u>to a minimum</u> of three additional potential Firstborn, Creator Wolf, Ravenous Wolf, and Soulless Wolf (thank you Blasphemies). All three of which could have Chronicles run around their formation, since they aren't part of the &quot;default&quot; setting. Two of which actually do have Plot Hooks around them, the third already having a 1st Ed write up.<br /> <br /> Hell without a Timeline of Tribe formation (Dark Eras may provide a rough one) we can make the Tribes has old or young as we want (within reason, it's safe to say that they are all at least several hundred years old if not a thousand).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T22:32:45-08:00","id":772092,"title":"","content":"Based on the stories it doesn't seem likely they were all created at the same time, and occurred gradually over a period of time when the totems happened to find a like-minded werewolf.<br /> <br /> It's possible future books will tell us about other tribes that have existed or will one day exist, but we're not allowed to get much in the way of spoilers for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T22:37:04-08:00","id":772095,"title":"","content":"The creation of a single tribe could have taken centuries. We know the first one likely was the Blood Talons and the last one the Iminir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T23:43:39-08:00","id":772122,"title":"","content":"[SPOILERS]<br /> Gaddammit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I don't understand is why it is now possible for a new tribal totem to be added to the werewolves, but it hasn't in the thousands of years werewolves have existed. </div> </div> </div>I'd say this is false though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":167,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","user":"nikink","date":". 11-23-2015, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T23:51:46-08:00","id":772126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Afro Luigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771556-fenris-ur-goals-in-basra-iraq?p=771747#post771747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like this! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Although I am tempted to reword it to &quot;that which has lingered too long&quot; so it covers institutions, customs, buildings, and beings. And then the Oath talks about how it's their duty to fill in the gaps, \u200bso we can keep some synergy with Destroyer Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also a good one. I'm inclined to suggest Purity or Cunning for the tribal Renown, but which one to go with is naturally likely to affect the general tenor of their hunting style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T06:49:27-08:00","id":772265,"title":"","content":"The qoute from 2ED corebook:<br /> <br /> <i>\u200bThis story is true. In the time before, when Father Wolf led his children in the hunt, Fenris-Ur had a twin Danu-Ur, she was called, the Creator Wolf. She alone could calm her brother's rages and convince him to quit the field. He alone could drive off the chattering spirits that swarmed around her and threatened to drive her mad. They were in balance then, but the Father's death tore them asunder. Now the Destroyer rages without end, and the Creator gibbers rapidly and spreads her madness like a plague.</i><br /> <br /> Kinda makes me thought about Pure's patron Rabid Wolf - he was a Wolf of True and driven to madness after Fathers Wolf death.<br /> <br /> Other option to that sounds to me as Maeljin's wanting to corrupt Creator Wolf - so if she would be purified of their madness and corruption, Maelinets and Bale Hounds sounds as good Favored Prey. Danu-Ur want to clean the world to create on &quot;clean slate&quot; and corruption of Lords of Wounds is worst that can be for her.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T03:24:43-08:00","id":789660,"title":"","content":"Sorry about the delay guys, I got super busy with exams.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771556-fenris-ur-goals-in-basra-iraq?p=772265#post772265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The qoute from 2ED corebook:<br /> Other option to that sounds to me as Maeljin's wanting to corrupt Creator Wolf - so if she would be purified of their madness and corruption, Maelinets and Bale Hounds sounds as good Favored Prey. Danu-Ur want to clean the world to create on &quot;clean slate&quot; and corruption of Lords of Wounds is worst that can be for her.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bHas much as I like this idea, I feel like it steps on the toes other tribes. So far the tribes have had clear divisions in what they hunt. Maelinets, could be argued to be the prey of the Bone Shadows, while Bale Hounds clearly would be the prey for the Blood Talon's. The only examples so far where the tribes hunt the same thing was a mix up in the stereotype section where an Iron Master get's a Leech Claimed confused with a Vampire.<br /> <br /> So I am going to go ahead and update the opening post with what I've got so far. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This is turning out awesome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T04:41:13-08:00","id":789675,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> I'd make favoured prey 'Those who are obsolete'. Much like a Pure tribe's favoured prey, the individuals get to define who fits the definition. (Also like the Pure, if they overreach they suffer consequences.)<br /> <br /> This also sets up a wonderful mystery/concern for Forsaken. Are the children of Dana-Ur forsaken or Pure?<br /> <br /> What if the new tribe declares the existing Uratha divide obsolete and works to build something new?<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T04:48:47-08:00","id":789676,"title":"","content":"I must admit, I would be tempted to make Creator Wolf a ruddy great Angel.<br /> <br /> On Tribal creation, it has been possible to make new Tribes prior to the modern day but you generally can't just go grab any old spirit and get it to serve as a Tribal totem. That role requires more than just Very Powerful Spirit, it needs to align with the hunt and the nature of the Uratha. Without the right spirit as totem it'll 'just' be a large and powerful Lodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T11:07:06-08:00","id":789828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771556-fenris-ur-goals-in-basra-iraq?p=789675#post789675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> I'd make favoured prey 'Those who are obsolete'. Much like a Pure tribe's favoured prey, the individuals get to define who fits the definition. (Also like the Pure, if they overreach they suffer consequences.)<br /> <br /> This also sets up a wonderful mystery/concern for Forsaken. Are the children of Dana-Ur forsaken or Pure?<br /> <br /> What if the new tribe declares the existing Uratha divide obsolete and works to build something new?<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> This is quite close to what we already have, but different enough in it's wording to create interesting idea. I do like the idea of an Upstart Tribe trying to tear down the Forsaken/Pure divide for a story though.<br /> <br /> @Acrozatarim: That would be immensely cruel to a hypothetical tribe. But Fun!<br /> <br /> So hypothetically would any spirit aligned to Hunting Work? Or would said Spirit need to be tied to wolves in some way?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T22:16:07-08:00","id":805017,"title":"","content":"So with the release of the information about playing the Pure I had an idea for how the Siskur-Dah for this hypothetical tribe would work if we use the prey of \u200b&quot;Those who've lingered to go long&quot;, &quot;that which has lingered too long&quot;, or &quot;Those who are obsolete&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe something like &quot;The Uratha senses the relative age of the prey and how relevant it is to the physical and social environment. As well as weak points in the structures physical structure or social network.&quot;<br /> <br /> My only problem with this is how close it is to the Ivory Claws benefit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T22:46:57-08:00","id":805030,"title":"","content":"I thought although it wasn't explicitly stated that it was kind of a given that Gurim-ur (Rabid wolf) was the modern remnant of what was once Danu-Ur (creator wolf), it was already alluded to in Lore of the Forsaken and Tribes of the Moon before the references in 2E. And also that one of the Werewolf writers is also a massive Sandman fan as there are too many parallels between delight/delirium and her elder sibling destruction and creator wolf/rabid wolf and its elder sibling destroyer wolf for me to write it off as coincidence. <br /> <br /> Going along with that idea I think bringing back Danu-Ur might require more creating a massive source of creation resonant essence and tricking Gurim-Ur into devouring it. The Idea would be to dilute the resonance of madness within Gurim-Ur and bring her back to her core concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T23:34:47-08:00","id":805051,"title":"","content":"as to what Danu-Ur's own tribe might look like, if in fact she decided to become patron of a tribe and following with the assumption that Danu-Ur is what become Gurim-Ur until he (possibly depending on your hypophetical chronicle) became cured of his madness well....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Favored renown:</b> Wisdom... the more things change the more things stay the same, wisdom always was the core of this totem, its what allowed her to talk down Fenris-Ur in the wildest of his rages, It was the core or herself that she held on when she became Gurim-Ur, its what he espoused even while in the throes of his grief stricken madness and most importantly its how he was saved and renewed, not with purity, cunning, glory or honour but with Wisdom. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tribal Vow: </b>this is going to be tricky as the tribal vows reflect an aspect of the tribe that won over the Firstborn as in the case of the blood talons, hunters in darkness and storm lords, or that the firstborn felt was necessary to keep the tribe grounded as in the case of the bone shadows and Iron masters.<br /> I think Danu-Ur would want her followers to be reluctant in using force as the primary approach for her tribe when solving their problems but would equally want a vow to stop them being all touchy feely when violence was necessary.<br /> Something like; let rashness not guide your strike nor allow indecision to withhold it<br /> Or something more succinct, poetic generally better phrased...you guys try<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sacred prey:</b> I think that &quot;those who are obsolete&quot; is a good starting point but we need to make sure were not treading too much on the toes of the Iron Masters as &quot;adapt or die&quot; is their tribal ethos and we need a clear differentiation.<br /> I was thinking something along the lines of &quot;they who would calcify and stagnate the world around you&quot; my logic is that Danu-Ur worked alongside and synergised well with Fenris-Ur as even wanton destruction ultimately only leaves more room for creation but my gut check is uncomfortable at it being too similar the hat to the Weaver/wyrm/wyld from Apocalypse (not that it\u2019s a bad thing but I\u2019m very much behind the idea of let\u2019s make forsaken its own thing). <br /> something that may perhaps strike a resonant note given Danu-Ur\u2019s past; those who would deny their own nature? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T23:38:10-08:00","id":805053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WelshBoi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771556-fenris-ur-goals-in-basra-iraq?p=805030#post805030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought although it wasn't explicitly stated that it was kind of a given that Gurim-ur (Rabid wolf) was the modern remnant of what was once Danu-Ur (creator wolf), it was already alluded to in Lore of the Forsaken and Tribes of the Moon before the references in 2E. And also that one of the Werewolf writers is also a massive Sandman fan as there are too many parallels between delight/delirium and her elder sibling destruction and creator wolf/rabid wolf and its elder sibling destroyer wolf for me to write it off as coincidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI must have missed those references, I'm going to have to go looking. Although that would match with the reference that says the &quot;Creator gibbers rabidly and spreads her madness like a plague&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WelshBoi\u200b</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going along with that idea I think bringing back Danu-Ur might require more creating a massive source of creation resonant essence and tricking Gurim-Ur into devouring it. The Idea would be to dilute the resonance of madness within Gurim-Ur and bring her back to her core concept</div> </div> </div> </div>This suggestion would be an interesting way to &quot;defeat&quot; a Pure tribe by changing it into something new. Although it does bring back the question what is Feris-Ur looking for in Basra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":4737,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","user":"Afro Luigi","date":".  Formating 01-10-2016, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T05:45:21-08:00","id":805173,"title":"","content":"I don't think Fenris-Ur knows what it's doing really, maybe this is just Destroyer Wolf lashing out in the fashion that only a firstborn with an entire tribe at its beck and howl really can lash out. Maybe Fenris-Ur feels that something is missing and that if he kicks up a big enough fuss the entire shadow will pay attention and maybe just maybe Danu-Ur will come back to save him from herself as she ways used to. <br /> <br /> <br /> Of course Danu-Ur isn't coming back because Gurim-Ur is too busy gibbering away and spreading its deranged gospel to the far reaches of existence.<br /> <br /> Fatima Dreams of Blood has been dreaming of a healed wound but she doesn't understand it (how does destruction contemplate creation?), other tribes has identified Fatima as a lynchpin holding the blood talons of Basra together and may seek to kidnap her.. If this where to happen and the other tribes learned of the dreams maybe they could help interpret them... Provided they could stop the blood talons from tearing their throats out first ...<br /> <br /> Fenris-ur is however building power, with only the blood talons hunting within the city the resonance is slowly being warped by destruction. And when every locus in the city has been so attuned Fenris-Ur will be able to unleash his Influence (capital I) on the area at a level previously unseen, even in the long memory of the hisil<br /> <br /> Bonus points maybe somewhere forgotten in the shadow of Basra is the way to a place-that-isn't that was once the den of creator-wolf (maybe if they where close danu-ur and debris-ur had a den together once)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":865,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","user":"WelshBoi","date":". 01-10-2016, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T07:22:49-08:00","id":805222,"title":"","content":"I don't agree that the Creator Wolf would like her tribe to destroy &quot;those that have lingered for too long&quot;. Remember, the Destroyer is Fenris. Danu(a)-Ur would be happy too see things lingering forever, since that proves her constructions are sturdy and &quot;right&quot;.<br /> <br /> What if this First Born had a connection with the Wolf-Blooded? They are the seeds that bloom into Uratha, and need to be protected if one wants to build a new generation of Werewolves. Her sacred prey could be anything that endangers the lives of Wolf-Blooded, like &quot;those who seek to end the blood of the wolf&quot;. This tribe could be focused on building and maintaining families of Wolf-Blooded, tracking their tells and building rites to increase the odds of them turning into Uratha. &quot;Wrong&quot; aspects of the tribe could be Uratha purposefully causing Lunacy to try and produce new Wolf-blooded.<br /> <br /> I also got the impression that Danu-Ur became Gurim-Ur at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T15:49:51-08:00","id":805554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771556-fenris-ur-goals-in-basra-iraq?p=805222#post805222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't agree that the Creator Wolf would like her tribe to destroy &quot;those that have lingered for too long&quot;. Remember, the Destroyer is Fenris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Defining hunting in this fashion makes this argument apply to all the Firstborn in general and therefore none of them in particular.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Danu(a)-Ur would be happy too see things lingering forever, since that proves her constructions are sturdy and &quot;right&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Things attempting to linger forever is kind of exactly why werewolves hunt most spirits for meddling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T16:53:50-08:00","id":805603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771556-fenris-ur-goals-in-basra-iraq?p=805554#post805554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Defining hunting in this fashion makes this argument apply to all the Firstborn in general and therefore none of them in particular.<br /> <br /> Things attempting to linger forever is kind of exactly why werewolves hunt most spirits for meddling.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you have to take into consideration that Fenris-Ur and Danu-Ur are both linked. Legend says they were the same once, and Danu is the aspect of creation, not destruction. Broadly defining your sacred prey as &quot;those who lingered for too long&quot; means that even Luna would be a valid target. The tribe would be full of terrorists blowing buildings that are too old, &quot;cleansing the land&quot;. Remember, Danu-Ur is still a spirit, and if it is a thing of creation, it will want creation, perhaps even going exactly against what Uratha are made for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T17:25:14-08:00","id":805630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/771556-fenris-ur-goals-in-basra-iraq?p=805603#post805603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you have to take into consideration that Fenris-Ur and Danu-Ur are both linked. Legend says they were the same once, and Danu is the aspect of creation, not destruction. Broadly defining your sacred prey as &quot;those who lingered for too long&quot; means that even Luna would be a valid target. The tribe would be full of terrorists blowing buildings that are too old, &quot;cleansing the land&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you define their sacred prey without consideration for the broader ethos it's part of and also veer into the nonsensical, sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember, Danu-Ur is still a spirit, and if it is a thing of creation, it will want creation, perhaps even going exactly against what Uratha are made for. </div> </div> </div>Spirits regularly attempt to cut their rivals off at the knees regardless of purview \u2014 Chris Allen put up a spirit of healing that frequently demands werewolves hurt people as payment for its services <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/794977-spirit-rite-the-pain-angel\">less than two weeks ago</a>. A spirit of creation that has no room or resources with which to facilitate creation isn't going to have any compunctions about having its work <i>last</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;Find the stories that make sense, and learn from them. Throw away stories that no longer apply. And if you need another legend, write another legend. Without adaptation, extinction. If the stories don\u2019t work for you, change them.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T17:54:53-08:00","id":805649,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, the real question is... what happened during the Iraq war that made Fenris-ur remember he was missing something? The corebook says it wasn't linked to any major event of the war, but that doesn't mean it wasn't triggered by SOMETHING that happened during the war and I'm guessing it's related to either the ruins of Bau, the god machine... or both.<br /> <br /> any ideas on what Fenris-Ur's trigger was?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}